Subject: [M156] Zero-initialize allocations in ZstdSourceStream::customMalloc

Original change's description:
> Zero-initialize allocations in ZstdSourceStream::customMalloc
>
> Update ZstdSourceStream::customMalloc in net/filter/zstd_source_stream.cc
> to allocate memory with calloc(1, size) instead of malloc(size).
> ZstdSourceStream passes custom allocation callbacks to
> ZSTD_createDCtx_advanced when constructing the zstd decompression
> context and its streaming buffers.
>
> During context initialization, zstd sets scalar and pointer fields of
> ZSTD_DCtx without clearing internal scratch buffers such as
> litExtraBuffer. When the streaming output ring buffer wraps and a
> subsequent sequence copies from litExtraBuffer at the wrapped prefix
> boundary, uninitialized bytes from a reused allocation could be copied
> into the output buffer. Zero-initializing allocations in customMalloc
> ensures deterministic initial decoder state. Added a unit test in
> net/filter/zstd_source_stream_unittest.cc covering both out-of-window
> and in-window match offsets after ring buffer wrap.
>
